<task id="032" project="email-communication-intelligence-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Golden end-to-end regression suite from R1 UAT misfile emails (ADR-038 KEEP path) — absorbs the FR-A3 formalization test</title>
    <phase>3 Pillar D — R1 carry-overs</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>TEST-MODIFYING override (CLAUDE.md §8): task creates/modifies tests/** and is tagged testing/integration-test → code-review + adr-check run UNCONDITIONALLY at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Test authoring against a known engine + pinned golden inputs; fully specified.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>pillar-d-independent</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds test files under tests/integration/seam/Communication/** — disjoint from 030/031 production files. Runs the engine as-is (green against current behavior); does not require 030/031 first.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>015</deps>
    <tags>testing,regression,integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Pin the R1 UAT misfile emails (PAT-942665, PAT-942404, REAL-2026-123456.02 + Invoice-10044725.pdf) as end-to-end regression tests under the ADR-038 KEEP path tests/integration/seam/Communication/**, reproducing and guarding the round-1/2/2b/3 outcomes. Absorb task 015's FR-A3 external-reply self-association test into this suite.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. BFF .NET 8, Communication Association Engine, ADR-038 seam-test discipline. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A CI-guarded seam suite under tests/integration/seam/Communication/** that drives the engine over the pinned golden emails and asserts: core-only auto-association; NO contact/invoice auto-file; Ambiguous on conflicting matters; and the FR-A3 external-reply self-association guarantee (custom headers stripped, parent regarding still inherited via ThreadContinuityRung). Suite is green against current engine behavior and fails loudly on regression.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>FR-D3. R1's UAT surfaced misfile modes now fixed in the rung ladder; without pinned regression tests those fixes can silently regress. The golden emails + expected outcomes are mined from R1 notes. FR-A3 (external-reply self-association) is already implemented in ThreadContinuityRung — task 015 (Pillar A) formalizes it; per spec its regression test folds here so there is one golden suite, not two.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Communication/GoldenMisfileRegressionTests.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/seam/Communication/ExternalReplySelfAssociationTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/061-uat-golden-emails.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/ThreadContinuityRung.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/IdentifierReverseLookupRung.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="015" status="pending">FR-A3 formalization (ThreadContinuityRung self-association) — its regression assertion is authored HERE per spec; if 015 changes the self-association surface, mirror it. Suite can be authored before 015 lands (guards current behavior) but the A3 test must reflect 015's formalized guarantee.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE = every new test file: land under a KEEP path (tests/integration/seam/Communication/**); these are MAINTAIN-class golden regression tests, NOT scaffolding — they survive /test-diet at project close. Ban Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, DI-registration, and ctor-null tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045">SCOPE = test harness: drive the engine through its real ladder entry point (no reaching into private rung internals to fake a verdict); assert the emitted association status/regarding.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = golden inputs: pin the exact R1 UAT emails + Invoice-10044725.pdf as fixtures checked into the test project; expected outcomes are the round-1/2/2b/3 verdicts (core-only auto-file; no contact/invoice auto-file; Ambiguous on conflicting matters).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE = §10 BFF hygiene: PRs modifying tests/** for Services/** must keep the suite green in CI; report publish-size is N/A for test-only changes but confirm the BFF still builds.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Golden seam regression + external-reply self-association</topic>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-024-polymorphic-resolver-pattern.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="seam-vertical-slice" location="docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md">tests/integration/seam/** vertical-slice-seam category — the DoD for dispatch-spine / engine changes; drive the real path, assert the observable verdict.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load this POML, spec FR-D3 + FR-A3, ADR-038, and R1 notes 061-*. Declare RIGOR LEVEL: FULL (TEST-MODIFYING override) with reason.</step>
    <step order="1">Mine projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/061-* for the exact golden emails, the Invoice-10044725.pdf attachment, and the round-1/2/2b/3 expected verdicts; pin them as test fixtures.</step>
    <step order="2">Author GoldenMisfileRegressionTests.cs driving the engine end-to-end per email: assert core-only auto-association; assert contact + invoice do NOT auto-file; assert Ambiguous when matters conflict.</step>
    <step order="3">Author ExternalReplySelfAssociationTests.cs (absorbing task 015's FR-A3 test): an external reply with Spaarke custom headers stripped still inherits the parent's regarding via ThreadContinuityRung on In-Reply-To/References.</step>
    <step order="4">Confirm all tests live under tests/integration/seam/Communication/** (KEEP path) and are wired into CI; run locally green against current engine behavior.</step>
    <step order="5">Confirm the BFF solution builds; run the suite; ensure no banned mock patterns.</step>
    <step order="6">Run code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5).</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="8">Document any deviation in projects/email-communication-intelligence-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the pinned golden outcomes cannot be reproduced against the current engine (a fixture drives a DIFFERENT verdict than the R1 notes record), STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — a divergence is either a real regression or a stale note, and must be adjudicated, not silently re-baselined.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + run the seam test suite.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Communication/GoldenMisfileRegressionTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/seam/Communication/ExternalReplySelfAssociationTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the PAT-942665 / PAT-942404 golden emails, when the engine runs, then only the core matter auto-associates (round-1/2 outcome).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given REAL-2026-123456.02 with Invoice-10044725.pdf, then neither the contact nor the invoice auto-files (round-2b outcome).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an email whose identifiers conflict across matters, then the verdict is Ambiguous (round-3 outcome), never a silent single auto-file.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an external reply to a Spaarke-originated email with custom headers stripped, then it inherits the parent's regarding via ThreadContinuityRung (FR-A3).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All new tests live under tests/integration/seam/Communication/** (KEEP path), are CI-guarded, and are green; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;/DI-registration/ctor-null tests; BFF build is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-D3 (absorbs FR-A3 regression). This suite is the CI guard behind Success Criteria #8. It runs the engine as-is; landing 030/031 must keep it green (031 is behavior-preserving; 030 changes indexing not association). Completion summary appended here when done.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
